# code-dupes.allow -- deliberate twins, with a budget and a reason.
# Format: fileA | fileB | budget | reason
# Generated by --baseline; every entry below is PRE-EXISTING duplication
# frozen so the gate only reports NEW or GROWING copies. The budget must
# EQUAL the measurement: a copy that shrank fails until its row says so.


# 2026-09-01: twins created or grown by the prevention-gate work. Reasons are
# specific; the two worth merging are recorded in docs/refactoring-backlog.md F3.

# --- PowerShell lane, frozen 2026-09-08 (ITEM 9) ------------------------------
# windows/ held 50,862 lines of .ps1/.psm1 that no structural gate scanned. The
# rows below are that lane's duplication AS MEASURED the day the gate learned to
# read PowerShell: nothing was fixed to get here, and nothing may grow from here.
# Same contract as every row above -- the budget EQUALS the measurement, so a
# shrink must be recorded and a pair that stops overlapping must be deleted.

# --- 2026-09-15, the six upstreamed helpers. Thirteen NEW pairs, each recorded at
# the measurement. Two real copies were given an owner first rather than budgeted:
# app_packaging_require_flatpak_tools and app_packaging_assert_flatpak_committed
# (the 73-shingle app-packaging.sh self-pair, gone), and t_stubbed_script in
# tests/test-harness.sh (which took the printf '%q' loop and the `bash -c` body
# out of the two new fixture runners). What is below is what remains after that.
# --- 2026-09-23, the rocm sdk layer's GPU loaders (Install-VulkanLoader.ps1, rocm-checks/GpuLoaders.ps1, the OpenCL
# ICD registration): twelve NEW pairs, each READ with --explain and recorded at the measurement.

