windows/scripts/build/Build-GstreamerFromSource.ps1 | windows/scripts/build/Build-GstreamerFromSource.ps1 | 18 | 2026-10-23: Shared Windows operations and fixtures; measured 33 -> 21. Historical review: reviewed 2026-09-09, READ: the 10-line run is a MESON INI SCHEMA, not logic -- the `[binaries] c=/cpp=/ar=/strip=/windres=/pkg-config=/cmake=` block of the cross file (Build-GstreamerFromSource.ps1:927) and of the native file (:985). Meson mandates the section and the key names; that is the shape a meson machine file has, and it cannot live anywhere but in the here-string that becomes the file. The two are DELIBERATELY independent and the code says why (#128 comment at :949): a cross file describes the host machine only, so the build machine had no C compiler at all and libnice/webrtc went missing -- the native file exists precisely to carry the SAME compilers WITHOUT --target. They then diverge completely (cross adds needs_exe_wrapper + [host_machine]; native adds [built-in options] link args, /vctoolsdir:, /winsdkdir:). One emitter would need a mode flag per section, and coupling them is the exact bug #128 fixed. Budget pinned
